[h1]Installation - Island Airfields 2.1[/h1]

For Revolution 1.6-19, subscribe to [url=https://steamcommunity.com/sharedfiles/filedetails/?id=3460002110]the original Revolution mod[/url] and enable [b]both Revolution and Island Airfields[/b]. Island Airfields is a separate addon and includes no Revolution files. Without Revolution, enable Island Airfields normally.
Windows / reviewed Carrier Command 2 1.5.18-r2 client. Requires CC2X SDK 0.8.1 client beta 1.

[url=https://github.com/Dioramawhois/-CC2X-island-airfields/blob/main/workshop/installation/README.md]Illustrated guide: screenshots and installation diagram[/url]

[h2]1. Subscribe to both items[/h2]
[list]
[*][url=https://steamcommunity.com/sharedfiles/filedetails/?id=3826940003]Island Airfields[/url] - the gameplay mod.
[*][url=https://steamcommunity.com/sharedfiles/filedetails/?id=3833014670]CC2X SDK[/url] - the shared runtime.
[/list]
Wait for Steam to finish downloading both. Subscribing downloads the SDK; the DLL still needs to be installed once.

[h2]2. Close the game and find the SDK DLL[/h2]
Open this folder inside your Steam library:
[code]steamapps/workshop/content/1489630/3833014670/content[/code]
Copy [b]dinput8.dll[/b].
[url=https://github.com/Dioramawhois/-CC2X-island-airfields/blob/main/workshop/installation/images/01-sdk-file.png]Screenshot 1: the SDK DLL[/url]

Alternatively, [url=https://github.com/Dioramawhois/Carrier-Command-2-extender/releases/download/0.8.1-client-beta.1/dinput8.dll]download the same DLL from this exact SDK release[/url].

[h2]3. Put it beside the game executable[/h2]
In Steam: [b]Library > Carrier Command 2 > gear icon > Manage > Browse local files[/b].
Copy the DLL itself into that folder:
[code]Carrier Command 2/
    carrier_command.exe
    dinput8.dll[/code]
Both files belong in the same folder. Keep a backup of an older identified CC2X runtime; check compatibility before replacing a different loader.
[url=https://github.com/Dioramawhois/-CC2X-island-airfields/blob/main/workshop/installation/images/02-game-folder.png]Screenshot 2: the game folder[/url]

[h2]4. Enable the mod[/h2]
Start the game, open [b]Mods[/b], enable [b]Island Airfields[/b], then restart.
After future SDK updates, repeat the DLL copy with the game closed. Steam does not update a manually copied DLL automatically.

[h2]Installation at a glance[/h2]
[code]Subscribe: Island Airfields + CC2X SDK
                    |
                    v
Close game -> copy SDK DLL beside carrier_command.exe
                    |
                    v
Start game -> Mods -> enable Island Airfields -> restart[/code]
[url=https://github.com/Dioramawhois/-CC2X-island-airfields/blob/main/workshop/installation/images/03-installation-flow.png]View the installation diagram[/url]

[h2]Updating an older setup[/h2]
The new version uses Lua/content and does not need a separate cc2x_island_airfields.dll. With the game closed, take only an older manually installed Island Airfields DLL out of its loading location, if you installed one. Keep the shared SDK and unrelated plugins. Enable one Island Airfields copy at a time.

Automatic installation through ModLoader requires a build that explicitly supports this exact SDK 0.8.1 runtime. Until your build supports it, use the manual route above. Other mods editing the map or vehicle-control screens require a compatible merge.

[h2]First check[/h2]
[list]
[*]Start single-player or an ordinary-host session. Custom with several starting islands is convenient for testing.
[*]Your airfields should be marked immediately in team colour.
[*]Give an airborne aircraft one waypoint near an owned airfield to land.
[*]Give a parked aircraft a new waypoint away from the island to launch.
[*]A replacement order before touchdown cancels the landing.
[/list]
Planes and helicopters are enabled by default. If something goes wrong, include cc2x.log from the game folder, game/SDK versions, enabled mods and reproduction steps.

Ordinary-host gameplay and map checks passed manual tests. A second remote client and dedicated servers remain unverified.
